  "description": "Change of use from Use Class C3 (dwelling house) to Use Class C4 (HMO-house in multiple occupation) involving hip to gable roof extension, rear dormer, front roof lights, with associated amenity, cycle and refuse storage.\r\r",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Ponders End",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-09T21:11:23.680Z",
  "street_name": "Scotland Green Road North",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed HMO by reason of its communal kitchen space layout with limited natural lighting and ventilation impacts within the kitchen that are associated with the proposed increased occupancy at the site, would represent a substandard and inappropriate form of accommodation which would not be capable of meeting the reasonable needs of its occupiers and would be detrimental to the standard of living of the occupants. The scheme therefore fails to provide an adequate standard of residential accommodation and it is contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Core Strategy Policies CP4 and CP30 (2010), Development Management Document Policies DMD5 and DMD37 (2014) as well as the NPPF (2026).",
    "Insufficient information has been submitted by way of a site specific Flood Risk Assessment to demonstrate that the development would be safe from flooding and that the two new ground floor bedrooms proposed would not be impacted by a flooding event. In addition, the submission fails to clarify the required Finished Floor Level (FFL) and Flood Evacuation Plan or SuDS mitigations within the scheme. The proposal is therefore contrary to the relevant flood-risk provisions of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies SI 12 and SI 13 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CP28 of the Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD 59, DMD 60 and DMD 61 of the Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed HMO development would intensify the residential use at the site, thereby resulting in an increase in comings and goings with associated noise impacts to the neighbouring occupiers without providing appropriate noise insulation and mitigation measures.  The scheme therefore fails to safeguard residential amenity and it is contrary to Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), Core Strategy Policies CP4 and CP30 (2010), Development Management Document Policies DMD5, DMD37 and DMD 68 (2014) as well as the NPPF (2026).",
    "The proposed development fails to provide sufficient details by way of a parking survey to assess the parking impacts of the development. It has therefore not been demonstrated that the proposal would not result in unacceptable parking stress on the surrounding highway network. The proposal is thereby contrary to Local Plan Policies CP24 and CP30 (2010), Development Management Plan Policy DMD45 (2014), Policies T5 and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021) and the guidance contained in the NPPF (2026)."
  ],
